270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Stemming and lemmatization both reduce words to a base form, but stemming uses simple rules to chop off endings, creating potentially nonsensical stems \(e.g., "running" -> "runn"\), making it fast but less accurate, while lemmatization uses context and dictionaries \(morphological analysis\) to find the actual dictionary word \(lemma\), like "better" -> "good," making it slower but more accurate for tasks needing meaning. Stemming is for speed \(search indexing\), lemmatization for accuracy \(sentiment analysis, translation\).  )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [0]
>>
